  "readmeFile": "Readme-package.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Android packaging and target frameworks changed in this release. Native SDK versions are unchanged.\n\n    BREAKING - Android target framework\n    * Android now targets net9.0-android35.0. net8.0-android is no longer supported; if you are still\n      on net8 stay on the previous release. Note that a net8 app will resolve the cross-platform\n      net8.0 dependency group, which carries the shared library only - it will not pick up the\n      Android implementation.\n\n    BREAKING - Android binding packages consolidated\n    * The 12 Android binding packages are retired and replaced by a single package,\n      XDev.Stripe.Android. If you referenced any of them directly, replace all of them with that one\n      reference: XDev.Stripe.Binding.Android.PaymentSheet, .Payments.Core, .Payments.Model,\n      .Payments.Ui.Core, .Stripe.Core, .Stripe.Ui.Core, .StripeAndroid, XDev.Stripe.Attestation,\n      XDev.Stripe.FinancialConnectionsCore, XDev.Stripe.FinancialConnectionsLite,\n      XDev.Stripe.HCaptcha, XDev.Stripe.Stripe3ds2Android.\n    * They were always an implementation detail - the supported surface is this meta-package plus\n      XDev.Stripe.PaymentSheet.Android.\n\n    Fixed\n    * Removed a dependency on XDev.Drewhamilton.Poko.PokoAnnotations. poko-annotations is a Kotlin\n      compile-time annotation that Stripe declares as a runtime dependency; it is not needed at\n      runtime and is no longer imposed on consumers.\n\n    .NET 10 / MAUI 10 consumers - no app-head pin needed\n    * The Android binding is still built for net9.0-android35.0 and holds AndroidX Navigation at the\n      pre-KMP-split 2.8.x generation, because .NET 9's Java stub generator crashes (XAGJS7000) on the\n      2.9.x type-forwarding facades. MAUI 10 supplies the rest of the Navigation family at 2.9.2.1,\n      which used to leave Compose as the straggler and fail the consumer's build with XA4212 on\n      AndroidX.Navigation.Compose.DialogNavigator/Destination.\n    * This release adds a net10.0-android36.0 dependency group that carries a corrective floor of\n      Xamarin.AndroidX.Navigation.Compose 2.9.2.1, so .NET 10 apps resolve a consistent Navigation\n      family automatically. If you previously added this pin at your app head, you can remove it:\n          <PackageReference Include=\"Xamarin.AndroidX.Navigation.Compose\" Version=\"2.9.2.1\" />\n    * net9 consumers are unaffected - they resolve the net9.0-android35.0 group and keep the 2.8.x\n      graph their toolchain requires.\n\n    Native SDK versions (unchanged)\n    * XDev.Stripe.PaymentSheet.Shared: 1.2.0\n    * XDev.Stripe.PaymentSheet.Android: com.stripe 22.6.1\n    * XDev.Stripe.PaymentSheet.iOS: 25.8.0",
